@Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5037

### Liveness probe -- always 200, no external dependencies
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/health
Accept: application/json

###

### Database readiness probe -- 200 if reachable, 503 + ProblemDetails if not
GET {{Api_HostAddress}}/health/db
Accept: application/json

###

### Register by e-mail -- passwordVerifier is a base64-encoded, client-derived Argon2id
### output (ADR-S02-02), never a plaintext password. The bytes below are a placeholder,
### not a real verifier.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "someone@example.com",
  "passwordVerifier": "AQIDBAUGBwgJCgsMDQ4PEBESExQVFhcYGRobHB0eHw==",
  "role": "professional"
}

###

### Login by e-mail -- returns the SAME response for an unknown e-mail and a wrong
### verifier (account enumeration mitigation).
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "someone@example.com",
  "passwordVerifier": "AQIDBAUGBwgJCgsMDQ4PEBESExQVFhcYGRobHB0eHw=="
}

###

### Register/login via Google -- requestedRole is only used when this e-mail has no
### account yet; otherwise the existing role wins (ADR-S02-01). Real Google ID token
### verification is not wired up yet (see Api/Accounts/GoogleIdentityProvider's TODO),
### so this call 401s against a real server today.
POST {{Api_HostAddress}}/auth/google
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "idToken": "replace-with-a-real-google-id-token",
  "requestedRole": "patient"
}

###
